Implemented Vercel Web Analytics for the React + Vite portfolio project.

## Changes Made

### 1. Installed @vercel/analytics Package
- Added `@vercel/analytics` version 2.0.1 to dependencies using npm
- Updated package.json and package-lock.json accordingly

### 2. Integrated Analytics Component
Modified: `src/App.tsx`
- Imported the Analytics component from '@vercel/analytics/react'
- Added the `<Analytics />` component at the end of the App component's JSX (inside the main div container)

### Implementation Details

Following the official Vercel documentation (https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart), I implemented the React-specific integration:

1. **Framework Identified**: React 19.2.6 with Vite 8.0.13
2. **Package Manager**: npm (detected from existing package-lock.json)
3. **Integration Pattern**: Added the Analytics component following React best practices
   - Imported from '@vercel/analytics/react' (React-specific export)
   - Placed component at the end of the App component, ensuring it tracks all page views
   - Positioned inside the root div to ensure proper DOM hierarchy

### Build Verification
- TypeScript compilation: ✓ Passed (no errors)
- Vite production build: ✓ Successful
- Bundle size: 343.59 kB (gzipped: 109.81 kB)
- No breaking changes introduced

### Next Steps for Deployment

To complete the Vercel Web Analytics setup:

1. **Enable Analytics in Vercel Dashboard**
   - Navigate to your project in the Vercel dashboard
   - Go to Analytics section in the sidebar
   - Click "Enable" to activate Web Analytics for this project

2. **Deploy to Vercel**
   - Deploy this code to Vercel (the analytics will automatically start tracking once deployed)
   - The Analytics component will inject the tracking script

3. **Verify Tracking**
   - After deployment, visit your site
   - Open browser DevTools > Network tab
   - Look for a request to `/_vercel/insights/view` or similar endpoint
   - This confirms analytics is actively tracking

### Files Modified
- `package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
- `package-lock.json` - Updated with new package and dependencies
- `src/App.tsx` - Added Analytics import and component

All changes preserve existing functionality and follow the project's code structure and conventions.
